---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Admit the crowd, or melt the shop" hint="60,000 fans want 20,000 tickets, and the shop can start about 100 new shoppers per second. Pick how the crowd is let in, and how fast, and watch the shop and the wait.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With <b>no queue</b>, all 60,000 fans refresh the shop at once: the load peaks near <b>517 times</b> what it can serve, it spends its time on timeouts, and only about <b>2,000</b> tickets are sold before the fans give up.</li>
    <li>Choose a <b>token queue at 100 per second</b>, the rate the shop can start: load stays at <b>1 times</b>, the 20,000 tickets sell out in <b>200 seconds</b> with no errors, and the median buyer waits about <b>98 seconds</b>. But only fans who arrived in the first ~6 seconds win.</li>
    <li>Switch to the <b>lottery</b>: the line is drawn after a 60-second window, so everyone who arrives in it has the same <b>39%</b> chance, at the cost of about <b>50 seconds</b> more median wait.</li>
    <li>Push the rate to <b>150</b>: the shop is overloaded, only 50 per second succeed, and 40,000 fans get an error page, so the sale takes <b>400 seconds</b>, twice as long. Admitting faster made it slower. At <b>20</b> per second nobody sees an error, but more than 32,000 fans give up waiting.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg wrb" data-wrb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>How the crowd is let in <select class="pg-in" data-strategy>
        <option value="none" selected>No queue: everyone refreshes the shop</option>
        <option value="lottery">Random lottery for the first 60 seconds</option>
        <option value="token">Token queue, first come first served</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Admission rate (people per second, queues only) <input type="range" min="10" max="300" step="10" value="100" data-rate /> <b data-rateval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Peak load on the shop</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Tickets sold</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Wait of the buyers</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Who got a ticket, by arrival time</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Fans who saw an error or gave up</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, one step per second: 60,000 fans arrive (36,000 in the first 10 seconds, 15,000 in the next 50, 9,000 over the next 4 minutes) for 20,000 tickets. The shop is healthy up to 100 new shoppers per second; between 100 and 200 its useful rate falls in a straight line to 5 per second, because it spends time on timeouts. Without a queue every waiting fan retries each second and gives up after 90 seconds. In a queue a fan waits up to 15 minutes. The lottery draws the order of everyone who arrived in the first 60 seconds, and later arrivals queue behind them.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wrb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const FANS = 60000; const STOCK = 20000; const CAP = 100; const QUEUE_PATIENCE = 900; const RETRY_PATIENCE = 90; const WINDOW = 60;
    const SEED = 2026; const MIN_GOODPUT = 0.05; // an overloaded shop still completes 5% of its capacity
    const ARR = { rushN: 36000, rushS: 10, midN: 51000, midS: 60, endS: 300 }; // 36,000 fans in the first 10 s, the next 15,000 by 60 s, the rest by 300 s
    const MAX_S = { none: 400, room: 3600 }; // simulation caps, seconds
    const P95 = 0.95; const OVERLOAD = 1.001; // peak load above capacity, allowing for rounding
    const goodput = (x: number) => (x <= CAP ? x : Math.max(MIN_GOODPUT * CAP, CAP * (2 - x / CAP)));
    const makeFans = () => {
      let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
      const ta = new Float64Array(FANS);
      for (let i = 0; i < FANS; i++) ta[i] = i < ARR.rushN ? rnd() * ARR.rushS : i < ARR.midN ? ARR.rushS + rnd() * (ARR.midS - ARR.rushS) : ARR.midS + rnd() * (ARR.endS - ARR.midS);
      ta.sort();
      return { ta, rnd };
    };
    function simulate(strategy: string, R: number) {
      const { ta, rnd } = makeFans();
      let sold = 0; let errors = 0; let peak = 0; let soldOutAt = -1; let gaveUp = 0;
      const got = new Uint8Array(FANS); const waits: number[] = [];
      const buy = (i: number, t: number) => { got[i] = 1; sold++; waits.push(t + 1 - ta[i]); };
      if (strategy === 'none') {
        let active: number[] = []; let next = 0; let acc = 0;
        for (let t = 0; t < MAX_S.none && sold < STOCK; t++) {
          while (next < FANS && ta[next] < t + 1) active.push(next++);
          const keep: number[] = [];
          for (const i of active) { if (t - ta[i] >= RETRY_PATIENCE) gaveUp++; else keep.push(i); }
          active = keep;
          const offered = active.length; if (!offered) continue;
          peak = Math.max(peak, offered / CAP);
          acc += goodput(offered); const K = Math.min(Math.floor(acc), offered, STOCK - sold); acc -= Math.floor(acc);
          for (let k = 0; k < K; k++) { const j = k + Math.floor(rnd() * (offered - k)); [active[k], active[j]] = [active[j], active[k]]; buy(active[k], t); }
          active = active.slice(K); errors += offered - K; if (sold >= STOCK) soldOutAt = t + 1;
        }
        gaveUp += active.length;
      } else {
        let pool: number[] = [];
        if (strategy === 'lottery') {
          let n = 0; while (n < FANS && ta[n] < WINDOW) n++;
          pool = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);
          for (let i = n - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(rnd() * (i + 1)); [pool[i], pool[j]] = [pool[j], pool[i]]; }
        }
        let p = 0; let acc = 0; const start = strategy === 'lottery' ? WINDOW : 0;
        const order = (k: number) => (k < pool.length ? pool[k] : k);
        for (let t = start; t < MAX_S.room && sold < STOCK && p < FANS; t++) {
          const ids: number[] = [];
          while (ids.length < R && p < FANS) { const i = order(p); if (ta[i] >= t + 1) break; p++; if (t + 1 - ta[i] > QUEUE_PATIENCE) { gaveUp++; continue; } ids.push(i); }
          if (!ids.length) continue;
          peak = Math.max(peak, ids.length / CAP);
          acc += goodput(ids.length); const K = Math.min(Math.floor(acc), ids.length, STOCK - sold); acc -= Math.floor(acc);
          ids.forEach((i, idx) => { if (idx < K) buy(i, t); });
          errors += ids.length - K; if (sold >= STOCK) soldOutAt = t + 1;
        }
      }
      waits.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      const med = waits.length ? waits[waits.length >> 1] : 0; const p95 = waits.length ? waits[Math.floor(waits.length * P95)] : 0;
      const share = (lo: number, hi: number) => { let n = 0; let s = 0; for (let i = 0; i < FANS; i++) if (ta[i] >= lo && ta[i] < hi) { n++; if (got[i] === 1) s++; } return n ? s / n : 0; };
      return { peak, sold, soldOutAt, med, p95, errors, gaveUp, a: share(0, ARR.rushS), b: share(ARR.rushS, ARR.midS), c: share(ARR.midS, ARR.endS) };
    }
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const pct = (x: number) => `${Math.round(x * 100)}%`;
    const cache = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof simulate>>();
    function draw() {
      const strategy = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-strategy]').value; const R = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rate]').value);
      q('[data-rateval]').textContent = String(R);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-rate]').disabled = strategy === 'none';
      const key = strategy === 'none' ? 'none' : `${strategy}:${R}`;
      let r = cache.get(key); if (!r) { r = simulate(strategy, R); cache.set(key, r); }
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${r.peak >= 10 ? fmt(r.peak) : r.peak.toFixed(1)} times`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = strategy === 'none' ? 'every waiting fan retries each second' : `${R} admitted per second against the ${CAP} the shop can start`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${fmt(r.sold)} of ${fmt(STOCK)}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = r.soldOutAt > 0 ? `sold out after ${fmt(r.soldOutAt)} seconds` : 'not sold out when the crowd was gone';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = r.sold ? `median ${fmt(r.med)} s` : 'no buyers';
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = r.sold ? `slowest 5% waited more than ${fmt(r.p95)} s` : 'nobody got through';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `first ${ARR.rushS} s: ${pct(r.a)}`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = `${ARR.rushS} to ${ARR.midS} s: ${pct(r.b)}, after ${ARR.midS} s: ${pct(r.c)}`;
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = `${fmt(r.errors)} errors`;
      q('[data-n5]').textContent = `${fmt(r.gaveUp)} fans gave up waiting`;
      const bad = r.peak > OVERLOAD || r.sold < STOCK;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.peak > OVERLOAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', r.sold >= STOCK ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b5]').style.setProperty('--c', r.errors + r.gaveUp > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      let text: string;
      if (strategy === 'none') text = `Everyone hits the shop at once. Load peaks at ${fmt(r.peak)} times its capacity, so it spends its effort on timeouts and sells only ${fmt(r.sold)} of ${fmt(STOCK)} tickets, mostly to whoever happened to get a retry through. ${fmt(r.errors)} requests failed.`;
      else if (r.peak > OVERLOAD) text = `Admitting ${R} per second is more than the shop can start (${CAP}). It slows down, only ${fmt(goodput(R))} per second succeed and ${fmt(r.errors)} fans get an error page, so ${r.sold >= STOCK ? `the sale takes ${fmt(r.soldOutAt)} seconds` : `only ${fmt(r.sold)} tickets are sold`}. Admitting faster made it worse, so the rate must follow what the backend can serve.`;
      else if (r.gaveUp > 0 || r.sold < STOCK) text = `The shop is safe, with no errors, but ${R} per second is slow: ${fmt(r.gaveUp)} fans gave up after waiting ${QUEUE_PATIENCE / 60} minutes and the tickets ${r.sold >= STOCK ? `took ${fmt(r.soldOutAt)} seconds to sell` : 'were not all sold'}. Spare capacity is wasted.`;
      else if (strategy === 'lottery') text = `The shop runs at ${r.peak.toFixed(1)} times capacity with no errors and sells out in ${fmt(r.soldOutAt)} seconds. Everyone who arrived in the first ${WINDOW} seconds had the same chance (${pct(r.a)} and ${pct(r.b)}), at the cost of a median wait of ${fmt(r.med)} seconds.`;
      else text = `The shop runs at ${r.peak.toFixed(1)} times capacity with no errors and sells out in ${fmt(r.soldOutAt)} seconds, median wait ${fmt(r.med)} seconds. It is orderly but strictly first come first served: ${pct(r.a)} of the first-10-second crowd won, and ${pct(r.b)} of those arriving a little later.`;
      out.textContent = text;
    }
    let pending = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (pending) return; pending = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { pending = false; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
